A||N||11||mope||-=My fiero peeeed on my girlfriend's leg=- HELP!||||1||
Z||000000||mope||06-28-2001||01:56 AM||||I just got all the aircondidtioning stuff all fixed in my car. Today we were driving around and there were little dropps of water comming out from under the passenger side of the dash. I think it was just condensation. why was it leeking there? what do i have to replace?<P>thanks<P>mope||||reg||1
Z||000001||RossT||06-28-2001||02:23 AM||||Sounds like the heater core is going out..<BR>replace it before you have a green swamp in your fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mope||06-28-2001||02:26 AM||||how much for a core if that is the problem?<BR>Who has a good one that they wanna sell me?<BR>What s the part number for a new one?<BR>Please tell me its something cheeper than a hundred bucks.!!!<P>thanks<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>mope||||reg||1
Z||000003||RossT||06-28-2001||02:32 AM||||Always replace with a new one.  The fierostore sells one for about $50.  You could also get one from your local parts store for a little less.  Its easy to replace. Not much skill needed.  At the last fiero show I was at a guy (who also won best of show) replaced his heater core in the parking lot the day before the show!!<P>But first make sure its your heater core.  Check to see if the fluid is green.  If its just starting to leak, you might only have a few drops of fluid in the carpet.  Its hard to see.  Take a white paper towel and blot your floor matt all over and see if you get drops of green on the paper towel.<P>also search this tech section on how to replace. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||RossT||06-28-2001||02:34 AM||||If it starts leaking real bad you can bypass the heater core by splicing the two lines together in the front trunk by the firewall.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||06-28-2001||02:41 AM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mope:<BR><B>I just got all the aircondidtioning stuff all fixed in my car. Today we were driving around and there were little dropps of water comming out from under the passenger side of the dash. I think it was just condensation. why was it leeking there? what do i have to replace?<P>thanks<P>mope</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>WAIT!! If the water was hot and smelled like anti-freeze it's the heater core. BUT if the water was just water and cold, while the A/C was running, Just in front of the flap vent by the heater core there is a tube that goes to teh outside. This is a drain for condensation when the A/C is on. (It's on the opposite side of the flap vent as the heater core) If the drain hole is clogged it will drip where the heater core is. Pull up the carpet, crawl back there and look up. You'll see the hose as it goes out the firewall. Remove it and stick a screwdriver thru the hole. Caution if clogged and you remove clog, water will flow out and into your face. Also the tube could be clogged .<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 06-28-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000006||mope||06-28-2001||10:12 AM||||i dont think its my heater core, it was clear not green, and it was cold, i am going to try to poke around and fix a clog.<P>thanks guys!||||reg||1
